{"files":[{"content":"#include <algorithm>\n#include <climits>\n#include <cstddef>\n#include <cstdio>\n#include <memory>\n\nint main() {\n    int n, s;\n    if (std::scanf(\"%d %d\", &n, &s) != 2) return 0;\n\n    const std::size_t stride = static_cast<std::size_t>(n) + 1;\n    const std::size_t tableSize = stride * stride;\n    std::unique_ptr<long long[]> prefix(new long long[tableSize]);\n\n    for (int c = 0; c <= n; ++c) prefix[c] = 0;\n    for (int r = 1; r <= n; ++r) prefix[static_cast<std::size_t>(r) * stride] = 0;\n\n    for (int r = 1; r <= n; ++r) {\n        const std::size_t rowBase = static_cast<std::size_t>(r) * stride;\n        for (int c = 1; c <= n; ++c) {\n            int value;\n            if (std::scanf(\"%d\", &value) != 1) return 0;\n            prefix[rowBase + c] = value;\n        }\n    }\n\n    #pragma omp parallel for schedule(static) if(n >= 256)\n    for (int r = 1; r <= n; ++r) {\n        const std::size_t rowBase = static_cast<std::size_t>(r) * stride;\n        long long running = 0;\n        for (int c = 1; c <= n; ++c) {\n            const std::size_t index = rowBase + c;\n            running += prefix[index];\n            prefix[index] = running;\n        }\n    }\n\n    const int tileWidth = 64;\n    const int tileCount = (n + tileWidth - 1) / tileWidth;\n    #pragma omp parallel for schedule(static) if(n >= 256)\n    for (int tile = 0; tile < tileCount; ++tile) {\n        const int firstColumn = 1 + tile * tileWidth;\n        const int lastColumn = std::min(n, firstColumn + tileWidth - 1);\n        long long vertical[tileWidth] = {};\n\n        for (int r = 1; r <= n; ++r) {\n            const std::size_t rowBase = static_cast<std::size_t>(r) * stride;\n            for (int c = firstColumn; c <= lastColumn; ++c) {\n                const int offset = c - firstColumn;\n                const std::size_t index = rowBase + c;\n                vertical[offset] += prefix[index];\n                prefix[index] = vertical[offset];\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    const int windows = n - s + 1;\n    long long best = LLONG_MIN;\n    #pragma omp parallel for collapse(2) schedule(static) reduction(max:best) if(windows >= 64)\n    for (int r = 0; r < windows; ++r) {\n        for (int c = 0; c < windows; ++c) {\n            const std::size_t bottomRight = static_cast<std::size_t>(r + s) * stride + (c + s);\n            const std::size_t topRight = static_cast<std::size_t>(r) * stride + (c + s);\n            const std::size_t bottomLeft = static_cast<std::size_t>(r + s) * stride + c;\n            const std::size_t topLeft = static_cast<std::size_t>(r) * stride + c;\n            const long long sum = prefix[bottomRight] - prefix[topRight] - prefix[bottomLeft] + prefix[topLeft];\n            if (sum > best) best = sum;\n        }\n    }\n\n    std::printf(\"%lld\\n\", best);\n    return 0;\n}\n","path":"src/solution.cpp"}],"hypothesis":"A padded 64-bit summed-area table makes each S×S window sum constant-time and independent, replacing the O(SN²) search with O(N²) construction and parallel window evaluation. Static scheduling and a max reduction should exploit the four CPU cores while tiled prefix construction limits strided-access costs.","notes":"The implementation uses one contiguous 64-bit table, about 512 MB at the largest valid N, in place of the original integer matrix. Prefix and window arithmetic use signed 64-bit values to preserve correctness for arbitrary signed entries. No candidate measurements are available.","research":{"queries":[],"urls":[]},"sources_kept":[],"transformations":["Read the matrix into a flattened, padded 64-bit table and construct horizontal then vertically tiled prefix sums in place.","Use static OpenMP work sharing for prefix construction, with serial execution for small matrices.","Evaluate all windows independently with a collapsed two-dimensional static work-sharing loop and a signed 64-bit maximum reduction." ]}